# sky130 (sky130_fd_sc_hd, @SYNTH_LIBERTY@): flip-flops and logic mapped to its cells,
# area of the cells and ABC's delay estimate of the longest path (stime, in yosys.log).
# Flattened by synth -flatten (yosys_synth.ys.in): one ABC run times the whole design.
# ABC maps the logic as written (strash only merges identical nodes, &nf maps for the best
# delay) and buffers and sizes gates (buffer, upsize, dnsize) as real flows do. No
# restructuring (fraig, scorr, dc2, dch, nor synth's own ABC): it optimizes area and
# turns fast carry logic into chains, measured: a 64-bit Kogge-Stone adder 7.8 ns with
# restructuring, 1.4 ns without.
log -stdout @SYNTH_NAME@ (@SYNTH_TECH@): mapping flip-flops to sky130 cells
read_liberty -lib @SYNTH_LIBERTY@
dfflibmap -liberty @SYNTH_LIBERTY@
log -stdout @SYNTH_NAME@ (@SYNTH_TECH@): mapping logic to sky130 cells, buffering, sizing (ABC)
abc -liberty @SYNTH_LIBERTY@ -script +strash;&get,-n;&nf;&put;buffer;upsize;dnsize;topo;stime,-p
opt_clean
log -stdout @SYNTH_NAME@ (@SYNTH_TECH@): statistics, netlist
tee -o stat.txt stat -liberty @SYNTH_LIBERTY@
write_verilog netlist.v
